e level BETWEEN blocks on one stream, including 1<->12 (straddling the lz4mid boundary) and out-of-range values that clamp.\n- row84/85: `LZ4_createStreamHC` + `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` contiguous chain, UNIFORM block sizes (row84) and RANDOM block sizes (row85), x cLevel sweep.\n- row86: `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` with each block in its OWN allocation => non-contiguous => `LZ4HC_setExternalDict`, x cLevel sweep. This also exercises the exported `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` (CONFIGS row 98).\n- row87: a chain whose total exceeds 64 KB, plus many blocks, to exercise the dictionary-reload path.\n- row89/90: `LZ4_loadDictHC` on a dict stream + `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary` on a working stream, then `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`. Cover COMPATIBLE levels (both <=2, or both >=3) with srcSize <= 4096 and > 4096, AND INCOMPATIBLE levels straddling the lz4mid boundary (e.g. dict stream at level 2, working stream at level 9, and vice versa). Also cover attaching NULL (detach).\n- row88: `LZ4_loadDictHC` dictSize sweep {0,1,3,4,8,9,64,1024,65535,65536,70000} x cLevel sweep, then a chain of blocks.\n- row91: `LZ4_saveDictHC` after a chain, maxDictSize in {0,1,3,4,64,1024,65536,70000,-1} x cLevel; compare return AND saved bytes AND that the stream stays usable identically afterwards.\n- row92: `LZ4_resetStreamHC` / `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` / `LZ4_initStreamHC` — reset then reuse; `resetStreamHC` and `initStreamHC` must be equivalent to a fresh stream.\n- row93: `LZ4_compress_HC_continue_destSize` chain with targetDestSize swept x cLevel.\n- row94/95/96/97: the deprecated wrappers (`LZ4_compressHC*`, `*_withStateHC`, `LZ4_compressHC_continue`, `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput_continue`, `LZ4_createHC`/`LZ4_freeHC`/`LZ4_slideInputBufferHC`/`LZ4_resetStreamStateHC`/`LZ4_sizeofStateHC`/`LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC`/`LZ4_compressionLevel_max`).\n- row99: every HC-produced block round-trips through `LZ4_decompress_safe` (or `_usingDict` when a dictionary was used) back to the original bytes.\n\nFor EVER