the C `LZ4_compress_HC` level 12 dereferences `src` even for `srcSize == 0` → SIGSEGV. Added `gen_src()` (same data, but always a real allocation with ≥64 readable zero bytes past `len`) and used it for every buffer whose address is handed to the C/Rust libraries. Stream-retained buffers (per-block outputs in row 65, ring buffers, `Comp` payloads, dictionaries) are all allocated before the loops that use them so nothing dangles.\n\n## (d) Not passing / caveats\nNothing left failing in my scope. One note: rows 66/67 deliberately mirror the compressor's and decoder's ring geometry so the streams stay valid (the compressor's overlap-truncated dictionary always excludes bytes the decoder has already overwritten); if that mirroring is ever changed, the \"decoded == original\" assertions in those two rows are the ones that would need rethinking.","usage":{"total_tokens":215894,"tool_uses":60,"duration_ms":1980981},"uuid":"f27fc2d1-e18c-409e-9186-76d68bb9ff11","session_id":"cf344e3a-451b-4037-95c8-f04f4dd0216c"}
