at the existing `tests/block_compress.rs` for the exact style/patterns to copy.\n\n## Exact C signatures (from c_src/include/lz4.h and c_src/src/lz4.c — verify by grepping)\n```\nint LZ4_decompress_safe(const char* src, char* dst, int compressedSize, int dstCapacity);\nint LZ4_decompress_safe_partial(const char* src, char* dst, int srcSize, int targetOutputSize, int dstCapacity);\nint LZ4_decompress_fast(const char* src, char* dst, int originalSize);\nint LZ4_uncompress(const char* source, char* dest, int outputSize);\nint LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize(const char* source, char* dest, int isize, int maxOutputSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k(const char* src, char* dst, int compressedSize, int maxDstSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k(const char* src, char* dst, int originalSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict(const char* src, char* dst, int srcSize, int dstCapacity, const char* dictStart, int dictSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict(const char* src, char* dst, int compressedSize, int targetOutputSize, int maxOutputSize, const char* dictStart, int dictSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict(const char* src, char* dst, int originalSize, const char* dictStart, int dictSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict(const char* source, char* dest, int compressedSize, int maxOutputSize, const void* dictStart, size_t dictSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict(const char* source, char* dest, int compressedSize, int targetOutputSize, int dstCapacity, const void* dictStart, size_t dictSize);\nLZ4_streamDecode_t* LZ4_createStreamDecode(void);\nint LZ4_freeStreamDecode(LZ4_streamDecode_t*);\nint LZ4_setStreamDecode(LZ4_streamDecode_t*, const char* dictionary, int dictSize);\nint LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize(int maxBlockSize);\nint LZ4_decompress_safe_continue(LZ4_streamDecode_t*, const char* src, char* dst, int srcSize, int dstCapacity);\nint LZ4_decompress_fast_continue(LZ4_streamDecode_t*, const char* src, char* dst, int originalSize);\n```\nUse the C library's OWN compressor (`LZ4_compress_default` / `LZ4_compress_fast` / `LZ4_compress_HC` / `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`) to produce the compressed input for these tests, so the payloads are valid.\n\n## Write ONE `#[test]` fn per CONFIGS.md row group, named `rowNN_...`:\n- row48: `LZ4_decompress_safe` round trip over `KEY_LENS` x `ALL_SHAPES`, exact dstCapacity.\n- row49: same but dstCapacity LARGER than the decoded size (+1, +7, +64, +4096).\n- row50: `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial` with targetOutputSize swept 0..decodedSize (use ~12 values incl. 0, 1, decoded-1, decoded, decoded+1) and dstCapacity == decodedSize.\n- row51: `_safe_partial` with targetOutputSize == dstCapacity < decodedSize (truncating).\n- row52: `_safe_partial` with targetOutputSize > dstCapacity.\n- row53: `LZ4_decompress_fast` with the exact originalSize.\n- row54: `LZ4_uncompress` (== decompress_fast) and `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize` (== decompress_safe).\n- row55/56: `LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k` / `LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k`. Set these up correctly: build a >= 64 KB contiguous buffer, compress a block that follows the 64 KB prefix using `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` on a stream primed with that prefix, then decode into a destination whose preceding 64 KB holds the same prefix bytes.\n- row57: `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict` with dictSize in {0,4,1024,65535,65536,70000} — note dictSize>=65536 disables the internal `checkOffset`.\n- row58: `_safe_usingDict` with a CONTIGUOUS dict (`dictStart+dictSize == dst`) vs a separate buffer.\n- row59: `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict` over the dict sweep x targetOutputSize sweep.\n- row60: `LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict`, contiguous and non-contiguous.\n- row61: `LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict` over the dict sweep.\n- row62: `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict` over dict x targetOutputSize sweep.\n- row63: `LZ4_setStreamDecode` + `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue`, linked-block stream, UNIFORM block sizes, decoding into one contiguous output buffer (compress side: `LZ4_createStream` + `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` on a contiguous source).\n- row64: same with RANDOM block sizes and many blocks.\n- row65: `_safe_continue` decoding each block into a SEPARATE output buffer, which forces the `forceExtDict` promotion path in the C.\n- row66: `_safe_continue` decoding into a ring buffer sized by `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize(maxBlockSize)`, wrapping around several times.\n- row67: `_safe_continue` exercising the small-prefix (prefixSize < 65535) and `doubleDict` paths — i.e. a ring/output buffer where the prefix has not yet reached 64 KB when a wrap occurs.\n- row68: `LZ4_decompress_fast_continue`, uniform and random block sizes.\n- row69: `LZ4_createStreamDecode`/`LZ4_freeStreamDecode` lifecycle plus a `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` value sweep (include negative, 0, 15, 16, LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE, LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE+1, and ~500 random i32 values).\n\nFor EVERY call: compare the C and Rust return values AND the produced output bytes byte-for-byte. Use MANY randomized inputs per row with a FIXED seed. Also assert the decoded bytes equal the original where the semantics guarantee it.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`. Do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n2. Watch out for DANGLING POINTERS in your own test code: LZ4 streams/streamDecode keep raw pointers into your buffers. Any `Vec` whose address a stream retains MUST outlive every later call on that stream. (A previous test had exactly this bug.)\n3. Build/iterate with: `timeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" ` then `timeout 600 cargo test --test block_decompress 2>&1 | tail -40`. Iterate until it COMPILES and RUNS.\n4. If C and Rust genuinely DIVERGE: the C is ALWAYS correct. Fix the RUST implementation in `src/*.rs` to match C exactly. Never weaken, delete, `#[ignore]`, or skip a test to make it pass. Never change expected values to match Rust.\n   - Common real bug class already found: the Rust panics with \"attempt to subtract with overflow\" where the C does signed `ptrdiff_t` pointer subtraction that can go negative — fix by using `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add` to match C, after confirming against the C source.\n5. In your FINAL REPORT, state: (a) the exact test names you created, (b) the final pass/fail count from the last `cargo test` run, (c) EVERY divergence found and the exact `src/*.rs` edit you made for it (file + line + before/after), (d) anything you could NOT get passing.\nDo not claim success without having actually run the tests.","agentId":"a14938690b2ac062b","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## (a) Test names created — `tests/block_decompress.rs` (new file, 1944 lines, 21 tests)\n\n| test fn | CONFIGS.md row |\n|---|---|\n| `row48_decompress_safe_exact_capacity` | 48 |\n| `row49_decompress_safe_oversized_capacity` | 49 (+1/+7/+64/+4096) |\n| `row50_partial_target_sweep` | 50 (~11 targets incl. 0, 1, n-1, n, n+1, n+64) |\n| `row51_partial_truncating` | 51 |\n| `row52_partial_target_above_capacity` | 52 |\n| `row53_decompress_fast` | 53 |\n| `row54_deprecated_uncompress_wrappers` | 54 (also cross-checked against `_fast`/`_safe`) |\n| `rows55_56_with_prefix_64k` | 55 + 56 |\n| `row57_safe_using_dict_size_sweep` | 57 |\n| `row58_safe_using_dict_contiguous_vs_separate` | 58 |\n| `row59_partial_using_dict` | 59 |\n| `row60_fast_using_dict` | 60 |\n| `row61_safe_force_ext_dict` | 61 |\n| `row62_partial_force_ext_dict` | 62 |\n| `row63_safe_continue_uniform_contiguous` | 63 (incl. `LZ4_setStreamDecode` with NULL, with a contiguous dict, and with a separate dict) |\n| `row64_safe_continue_random_blocks` | 64 (incl. zero-length blocks mid-chain) |\n| `row65_safe_continue_separate_buffers` | 65 |\n| `row66_safe_continue_ring_buffer` | 66 (≥3 wraps per config, ring from `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize`) |\n| `row67_safe_continue_small_prefix_and_double_di