{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ofnqwlqjytvvhkz4kjzb3ij6yhu23wim7cjwfum4rewehqbslgha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01JvXNt9aRES5zbTZ8WW4Y7A","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Mleh93/translated_rust/tests/hc.rs","old_string":"/// `LZ4_compressBound(n)`, never 0 (so a `notLimited` call always has room).\nfn bound_of(bound: &FnBound, n: usize) -> usize {\n    unsafe { bound(n as c_int) }.max(1) as usize\n}","new_string":"/// `LZ4_compressBound(n)`, never 0 (so a `notLimited` call always has room).\nfn bound_of(bound: &FnBound, n: usize) -> usize {\n    unsafe { bound(n as c_int) }.max(1) as usize\n}\n\n/// `gen_data`, but the buffer is ALWAYS backed by a real allocation, so even a\n/// zero-length source has a *valid* address.\n///\n/// `Vec::<u8>::as_ptr()` on a zero-capacity vector returns the dangling\n/// pointer `0x1`. Every HC parser computes `src + srcSize - MFLIMIT` (and\n/// friends) up front; around address `0x1` those wrap to the top of the address\n/// space, the `ip <= mflimit` guard then passes, and the C `.so` walks off into\n/// unmapped memory. That is a defect of the *caller*, not of either library, so\n/// never hand a dangling pointer to the API.\nfn gen_src(shape: Shape, len: usize, rng: &mut Rng) -> Vec<u8> {\n    let mut v = gen_data(shape, len, rng);\n    if v.capacity() < 64 {\n        v.reserve(64);\n    }\n    v\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":492,"cache_read_input_tokens":185012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":492,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y4ushvz3xgK5E6YkGpuQp4","session_id":"cf344e3a-451b-4037-95c8-f04f4dd0216c","uuid":"fa8fc4d2-439d-4381-8ef5-4b417b490279","timestamp