t_hc` still compares `LZ4_saveDictHC`'s return + saved bytes for `prefixSize == 0` and only skips the follow-up compress. Documented inline.\n- Also documented inline: zero-length sources must not be passed as `Vec::as_ptr()` of a zero-capacity `Vec` (dangling `0x1`) — the HC parsers precompute `src + srcSize - MFLIMIT`, which wraps around `0x1` and makes the **C** walk off into unmapped memory. The test's `gen_src()` helper guarantees a real allocation.\n- The 2 GB index-reload branch (`lz4hc.c:1695`) is unreachable without a >2 GB stream; row87 covers the 64 KB-crossing + `saveDictHC` re-anchor + >64 KB `loadDictHC` reload paths instead.\n\nNo files other than `tests/hc.rs` and `src/lz4hc.rs` were changed (`rustfmt` incidentally reformatted one `assert!` in `tests/common/mod.rs`; I reverted it byte-for-byte)."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: adbca12dbe5db1eaa (use SendMessage with to: 'adbca12dbe5db1eaa', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 248774\ntool_uses: 114\nduration_ms: 4129292</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf344e3a-451b-4037-95c8-f04f4dd0216c","uuid":"6694200b-17dc-4371-9e92-fefe2dc9f0bf","timestamp":"2026-08-14T19:25:25.078Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Mleh93/translated_rust\n\nWrite a NEW file `tests/hc.rs` — differential tests comparing the C `.so` against the Rust `.so` for lz4hc.c (the HIGH-COMPRESSION API).\n\n## Harness (already exists — read `tests/common/mod.rs` first, do NOT modify it)\n- `mod common; use common::*;`\n- `sym!(name, \"C_SYMBOL\", FnType);` declares `name.0` = C fn, `name.1` = Rust fn; call as `name.0(args)` inside `unsafe`.\n- Helpers: `Rng::new(seed)`, `rng.range(lo,hi)`, `rng.below(n)`, `rng.next_u8/u32/u64`,\n  `gen_data(Shape, len, &mut rng) -> Vec<u8>`, `ALL_SHAPES`, `KEY_LENS`, `SMALL_LENS`,\n  `assert_bytes_eq`, `assert_ret_eq`, `assert_out_eq(cn,cbuf,rn,rbuf,ctx)`,\n  `Aligned::new(n)` + `.ptr()` for 8-byte-aligned state, `SIZEOF_LZ4_STREAMHC_T` (262200).\n- Copy the exact style/patterns from the existing `tests/block_compress.rs`.\n\n## Exact C signatures (verify by grepping c_src/include/lz4hc.h and c_src/src/lz4hc.c)\n```\nint LZ4_compress_HC(const char* src, char* dst, int srcSize, int dstCapacity, int compressionLevel);\nint LZ4_sizeofStateHC(void);\nint LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC(void* stateHC, const char* src, char* dst, int srcSize, int maxDstSize, int compressionLevel);\nint LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset(void* state, const char* src, char* dst, int srcSize, int dstCapacity, int compressionLevel);\nint LZ4_compress_HC_destSize(void* stateHC, const char* src, char* dst, int* srcSizePtr, int targetDstSize, int compressionLevel);\nLZ4_streamHC_t* LZ4_createStreamHC(void);\nint LZ4_freeStreamHC(LZ4_streamHC_t*);\nLZ4_streamHC_t* LZ4_initStreamHC(void* buffer, size_t size);\nvoid LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast(LZ4_streamHC_t*, int compressionLevel);\nvoid LZ4_resetStreamHC(LZ4_streamHC_t*, int compressionLevel);\nint LZ4_loadDictHC(LZ4_streamHC_t*, const char* dictionary, int dictSize);\nvoid LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary(LZ4_streamHC_t* working_stream, const LZ4_streamHC_t* dictionary_stream);\nint LZ4_compress_HC_continue(LZ4_streamHC_t*, const char* src, char* dst, int srcSize, int maxDstSize);\nint LZ4_compress_HC_continue_destSize(LZ4_streamHC_t*, const char* src, char* dst, int* srcSizePtr, int targetDstSize);\nint LZ4_saveDictHC(LZ4_streamHC_t*, char* safeBuffer, int maxDictSize);\nvoid LZ4_setCompressionLevel(LZ4_streamHC_t*, int compressionLevel);\nvoid LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed(LZ4_streamHC_t*, int favor);\nint LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC(void);\nint LZ4_resetStreamStateHC(void* state, char* inputBuffer);\nvoid* LZ4_createHC(const char* inputBuffer);\nint LZ4_freeHC(void* LZ4HC_Data);\nchar* LZ4_slideInputBufferHC(void* LZ4HC_Data);\nint LZ4_compressHC(const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize);\nint LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput(const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize, int maxOutputSize);\nint LZ4_compressHC2(const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize, int cLevel);\nint LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput(const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize, int maxOutputSize, int cLevel);\nint LZ4_compressHC_withStateHC(void* state, const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize);\nint LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput_withStateHC(void* state, const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize, int maxOutputSize);\nint LZ4_compressHC2_withStateHC(void* state, const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize, int cLevel);\nint LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput_withStateHC(void* state, const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize, int maxOutputSize, int cLevel);\nint LZ4_compressHC_continue(void* LZ4HC_Data, const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize);\nint LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput_continue(void* LZ4HC_Data, const char* source, char* dest, int inputSize, int maxOutputSize);\nint LZ4_compressionLevel_max(void);   /* exported from lz4frame */\n```\n`LZ4_compressBound` and `LZ4_decompress_safe`/`LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict` (from lz4.h) are also available for sizing and round-trip verification.\n\n## Compression-level classes the C branches on (CRITICAL — must all be covered)\n`LZ4HC_getCLevelParams`: `cLevel < 1` -> clamped to 9; `cLevel > 12` -> clamped to 12; `cLevel == 1` is ACCEPTED (not clamped to 2). Levels 1-2 use the `lz4mid` algorithm, 3-9 the HC chain, 10-12 the optimal parser (`LZ4HC_CLEVEL_OPT_MIN`). `favorDecSpeed` is only consulted at levels >= 10.\n\n## Write ONE `#[test]` fn per CONFIGS.md row group, named `rowNN_...`:\n- row70/71/72: `LZ4_compress_HC` with cLevel 1..12 (plus 0, -1, 13, 100 which clamp) x `ALL_SHAPES` x input lengths. Use `KEY_LENS` for levels 1-9 and `SMALL_LENS` for levels 10-12 (the optimal parser is slow in a debug build). Verify return code + bytes + round trip via `LZ4_decompress_safe`.\n- row73: cLevel sweep x `limitedOutput` dstCapacity sweep (0,1,2,5, natural-1, natural, natural/2, natural/4, plus random values).\n- row74/75/76: dedicated tests pinning levels {1,2}, {3..9}, {10,11,12} across all shapes.\n- row77: `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC` with caller-owned aligned state x cLevel sweep.\n- row78: `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset` — a FRESH state and then the SAME state REUSED across many calls (the fast-reset path) x cLevel sweep.\n- row79/80: `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize` (fillOutput) with targetDstSize swept x cLevel 1..12; make sure the sweep produces truncation so the \"dest overflow salvage\" paths at all three level classes are hit. Compare the returned size AND the updated `*srcSizePtr` AND the bytes.\n- row81/82: `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed(stream, favor)` with favor 0 and 1 (and nonzero values like -1, 12345) x cLevel {10,11,12} (row81) and {1..9} (row82), then `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`.\n- row83: `LZ4_setCompressionLevel` changing the level BETWEEN blocks on one stream, including 1<->12 (straddling the lz4mid boundary) and out-of-range values that clamp.\n- row84/85: `LZ4_createStreamHC` + `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` contiguous chain, UNIFORM block sizes (row84) and RANDOM block sizes (row85), x cLevel sweep.\n- row86: `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` with each block in its OWN allocation => non-contiguous => `LZ4HC_setExternalDict`, x cLevel sweep. This also exercises the exported `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` (CONFIGS row 98).\n- row87: a chain whose total exceeds 64 KB, plus many blocks, to exercise the dictionary-reload path.\n- row89/90: `LZ4_loadDictHC` on a dict stream + `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary` on a working stream, then `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`. Cover COMPATIBLE levels (both <=2, or both >=3) with srcSize <= 4096 and > 4096, AND INCOMPATIBLE levels straddling the lz4mid boundary (e.g. dict stream at level 2, working stream at level 9, and vice versa). Also cover attaching NULL (detach).\n- row88: `LZ4_loadDictHC` dictSize sweep {0,1,3,4,8,9,64,1024,65535,65536,70000} x cLevel sweep, then a chain of blocks.\n- row91: `LZ4_saveDictHC` after a chain, maxDictSize in {0,1,3,4,64,1024,65536,70000,-1} x cLevel; compare return AND saved bytes AND that the stream stays usable identically afterwards.\n- row92: `LZ4_resetStreamHC` / `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` / `LZ4_initStreamHC` — reset then reuse; `resetStreamHC` and `initStreamHC` must be equivalent to a fresh stream.\n- row93: `LZ4_compress_HC_continue_destSize` chain with targetDestSize swept x cLevel.\n- row94/95/96/97: the deprecated wrappers (`LZ4_compressHC*`, `*_withStateHC`, `LZ4_compressHC_continue`, `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput_continue`, `LZ4_createHC`/`LZ4_freeHC`/`LZ4_slideInputBufferHC`/`LZ4_resetStreamStateHC`/`LZ4_sizeofStateHC`/`LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC`/`LZ4_compressionLevel_max`).\n- row99: every HC-produced block round-trips through `LZ4_decompress_safe` (or `_usingDict` when a dictionary was used) back to the original bytes.\n\nFor EVERY call: compare the C and Rust return values AND the produced output bytes byte-for-byte. Use MANY randomized inputs per row with a FIXED seed.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`. Do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`, or `tests/block_compress.rs`.\n2. Watch out for DANGLING POINTERS in your own test code: HC streams keep raw pointers into your source buffers (`prefixStart`, `end`, `dictionary`). Any `Vec` whose address a stream retains MUST outlive every later call on that stream, including `LZ4_saveDictHC`. (A previous test had exactly this bug and it looked like a library divergence.)\n3. Keep the total runtime under ~5 minutes: levels 10-12 with the optimal parser are slow in a DEBUG build, so use `SMALL_LENS` and modest iteration counts for those.\n4. Build/iterate with: `timeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"` then `timeout 600 cargo test --test hc 2>&1 | tail -40`. Iterate until it COMPILES and RUNS.\n5. If C and Rust genuinely DIVERGE: the C is ALWAYS correct. Fix the RUST implementation in `src/lz4hc.rs` (or `src/lz4.rs`) to match C exactly. Never weaken, delete, `#[ignore]`, or skip a test to make it pass. Never change an expected value to match Rust.\n   - Real bug class already found elsewhere: the Rust panics \"attempt to subtract with overflow\" where C does signed `ptrdiff_t` pointer subtraction that can go negative — fix with `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add` after confirming against the C source.\n6. In your FINAL REPORT state: (a) the exact test names created, (b) the final pass/fail count from your last `cargo test` run, (c) EVERY divergence found with the exact `src/*.rs` edit (file + line + before/after), (d) anything you could NOT get passing.\nDo not claim success without having actually run the tests.","agentId":"adbca12dbe5db1eaa","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. Final state verified.\n\n## What was done\n\nCreated **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Mleh93/translated_rust/tests/hc.rs`** (2144 lines) — differential tests for the lz4hc.c high-compression API, comparing the C `.so` against the Rust `.so` on return value **and** output bytes for every call, with fixed seeds.\n\n### (a) Test names created (20 `#[test]` fns)\n`rows70_72_compress_hc_levels_shapes_sizes`, `row73_compress_hc_limited_output_capacity_sweep`, `rows74_76_level_classes`, `row77_compress_hc_ext_state`, `row78_compress_hc_ext_state_fast_reset`, `rows79_80_compress_hc_dest_size`, `row81_favor_decompression_speed_optimal_levels`, `row82_favor_decompression_speed_ignored_levels`, `row83_set_compression_level_between_blocks`, `rows84_85_continue_contiguous_chains`, `row86_continue_external_dict`, `row87_long_chain_over_64k`, `row88_load_dict_hc_size_sweep`, `rows89_90_attach_hc_dictionary`, `row91_save_dict_hc`, `row92_reset_paths`, `row93_continue_dest_size_chain`, `rows94_95_deprecated_oneshots`, `rows96_97_deprecated_streaming`, `row99_round_trip_all_apis`.\n\nAll 36 HC symbols are exercised. Note: `LZ4_compressionLevel_max` does **not** exist in either `.so`; the exported symbol is `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max` (used, asserted == 12). `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` is exported but takes/returns internal types, so it is covered indirectly (levels 1-2 + 3-12 attached-dict paths in rows89_90 — that path is what surfaced divergence #2 below).\n\n### (b) Final result\n`cargo test --test hc` → **`test result: ok. 20 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored`**, 234.8s (235s wall, under the 5-minute budget).\n\n### (c) Divergences found — all fixed in `src/lz4hc.rs` (C is authoritative)\n1. **`LZ4MID_compress` (levels 1-2), line 583-589** — `ilimitIdx` overflow panic for any input shorter than `LZ4MID_HASHSIZE` (8). C: `const U32 ilimitIdx = (U32)(ilimit - prefixPtr) + prefixIdx;` (negative ptrdiff → U32 wrap, harmless because the `*srcSizePtr < LZ4_minLength` guard follows).\n   - before: `let ilimitIdx = (ilimit as usize - prefixPtr as usize) as u32 + prefixIdx;`\n   - after: `let ilimitIdx = ((ilimit as usize).wrapping_sub(prefixPtr as usize) as u32).wrapping_add(prefixIdx);`\n2. **`LZ4HC_InsertAndGetWiderMatch` dictCtx chain walk, lines 1114-1118** — underflow panic on the attached-dictionary path (rows 89/90). C (lz4hc.c:2091-2093) relies on U32 wrap; the `ipIndex - matchIndex <= LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX` guard rejects the wrapped value. The standalone `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` (line 367-368) already used `wrapping_sub`, so this inlined copy was inconsistent.\n   - before: `dictMatchIndex -= nextOffset; matchIndex -= nextOffset;`\n   - after: `dictMatchIndex = dictMatchIndex.wrapping_sub(nextOffset); matchIndex = matchIndex.wrapping_sub(nextOffset);`\n3. **`LZ4HC_compress_optimal` `_dest_overflow` handler, line ~1488** — real behavioural divergence (not a panic): `oend = oend.wrapping_add(LASTLITERALS);` was executed before calling `hc_last_literals`, which restores `oend` itself, double-restoring it. C's `_dest_overflow` falls through to `_last_literals`, where the restore happens exactly once. Symptom: `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize(lvl=10, len=13, tgt=1)` returned `*srcSizePtr = 5` vs C's `0` (salvaged literal run inflated by 5 bytes). Fixed by deleting that line (the lz4mid and hash-chain handlers were already correct).\n\n### (d) Not covered (with reason)\n- **`LZ4_saveDictHC` on a stream that was never used, followed by a compress.** The C `.so` **segfaults** here too (verified by driving C-only): the save re-anchors with `dictLimit == lowLimit == 0`, so the reserved \"no entry\" index 0 becomes a valid match index and `matchIndex -= DELTANEXTU16(...)` underflows into a wild pointer. Genuine UB in both, so not differentially testable (ERRORS.md UB appendix); `row91_save_dict_hc` still compares `LZ4_saveDictHC`'s return + saved bytes for `prefixSize == 0` and only skips the follow-up compress. Documented inline.\n- Also documented inline: zero-length sources must not be passed as `Vec::as_ptr()` of a zero-capacity `Vec` (dangling `0x1`) — the HC parsers precompute `src + srcSize - MFLIMIT`, which wraps around `0x1` and makes the **C** walk off into unmapped memory. The test's `gen_src()` helper guarantees a real allocation.\n- The 2 GB index-reload branch (`lz4hc.c:1695`) is unreachable without a >2 GB stream; row87 covers the 64 KB-crossing + `saveDictHC` re-anchor + >64 KB `loadDictHC` reload paths instead.\n\nNo files other than `tests/hc.rs` and `src/lz4hc.rs` were changed (`rustfmt` incidentally reformatted one `assert!` in `tests/common/mod.rs`; I reverted it byte-for-byte)."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":4129292,"totalTokens":248774,"totalToolUseCount":114,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":246084,"output_tokens":2141,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":547},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":85,"editFileCount":22,"linesAdded":2507,"linesRemoved":126,"otherToolCount":0}}}
