ize == 0) => 0, NOT an error. With buffered data and\n  cStage != 1 => `lz4f_err(20)`. dstCapacity < tmpInSize+8 => `lz4f_err(11)`.\n- `LZ4F_compressEnd` dstCapacity too small for the endMark => `lz4f_err(11)`; with\n  contentChecksumEnabled needing 8 => `lz4f_err(11)`; declared `contentSize` != bytes actually fed\n  => `lz4f_err(14)`; on a fresh never-begun cctx => 4 (succeeds).\n- `LZ4F_compressBound`/`LZ4F_compressFrameBound` with an INVALID blockSizeID return a huge garbage\n  value (the C does not error-check `LZ4F_getBlockSize` there) — assert C and Rust produce the\n  IDENTICAL garbage.\n- `LZ4F_compressFrame` with dstCapacity < `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` => `lz4f_err(11)`; exactly at it => success.\n- `LZ4F_headerSize`: NULL src => `lz4f_err(15)`; srcSize 0..4 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic =>\n  `lz4f_err(13)`; skippable magic (all 16 values 0x184D2A50..5F) => 8; valid => 7/11/15/19.\n- `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`: srcSize < 5 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic => `lz4f_err(13)`; partial header\n  (>=5 but < hSize) => `lz4f_err(12)`; FLG bit1 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; FLG version field in {0,2,3}\n  => `lz4f_err(6)`; BD bit7 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; BD blockSizeID in {0,1,2,3} => `lz4f_err(2)`;\n  BD low nibble != 0 => `lz4f_err(8)`; wrong header-checksum byte => `lz4f_err(17)`;\n  called after feeding a PARTIAL header to `LZ4F_decompress` => `lz4f_err(19)`.\n  In each case also assert `*srcSizePtr` is set identically (the C zeroes it on these errors).\n  Build these headers BY HAND (magic + FLG + BD + optional 8-byte contentSize + optional 4-byte\n  dictID + header-checksum byte `(XXH32(hdr, n, 0) >> 8) & 0xFF`, using the library's own\n  `LZ4_XXH32` to compute it) so each field is corrupted in isolation.\n- `LZ4F_decompress`: srcSize 0 on a fresh dctx => 7 (a hint, not an error); every header error\n  above forwarded; block header size > maxBlockSize => `lz4f_err(2)`; corrupt compressed block\n  payload => `lz4f_err(16)`; wrong block checksum on a COMPRESSED block => `lz4f_err(7