lue to match Rust.\n   Real bug classes already found in this project: (i) Rust panicking \"attempt to subtract/add with\n   overflow\" where C does signed `ptrdiff_t` pointer arithmetic or relies on U32 wraparound — fix\n   with `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add` after confirming against the C source; (ii) a restore\n   statement executed twice on an error path.\n6. FINAL REPORT must state: (a) exact test names created in each file, (b) the pass/fail counts\n   from your last actual `cargo test` run of BOTH binaries, (c) EVERY divergence found with the\n   precise `src/*.rs` edit (file + line + before/after), (d) anything you could NOT get passing and why.\nDo not claim success without having actually run both test binaries.","uuid":"7ce36417-5bc2-44de-a16b-d3fb9b25f111","session_id":"cf344e3a-451b-4037-95c8-f04f4dd0216c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Mleh93/translated_rust\n\nWrite TWO new files:\n- `tests/frame.rs` — VALID-PATH differential tests for lz4frame.c (CONFIGS.md rows 100-143)\n- `tests/frame_errors.rs` — ERROR-PATH differential tests for lz4frame.c (ERRORS.md rows 125-203)\n\nBoth compare the C `.so` against the Rust `.so` through their exported symbols.\n\n## Harness (already exists — read `tests/common/mod.rs` FIRST; do NOT modify it)\n- `mod common; use common::*;`\n- `sym!(name, \"C_SYMBOL\", FnType);` declares `name.0` = C fn, `name.1` = Rust fn; call as `name.0(args)` inside `unsafe`.\n- Helpers: `Rng::new(seed)`, `rng.range(lo,hi)`, `rng.below(n)`, `rng.next_u8/u32/u64`,\n  `gen_data(Shape, len, &mut rng) -> Vec<u8>`, `ALL_SHAPES`, `KEY_LENS`, `SMALL_LENS`,\n  `assert_bytes_eq`, `assert_ret_eq`, `assert_out_eq`, `assert_sz_eq(cn,cbuf,rn,rbuf,ctx)`,\n  `is_lz4f_error(code) -> bool` (mirrors `LZ4F_isError`), `lz4f_err(n) -> usize` (= `(size_t)-n`),\n  `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX` (19), `LZ4F_VERSION` (100), `LZ4F_MAGICNUMBER` (0x184D2204).\n- Copy the style/patterns from the existing `tests/block_compress.rs` and `tests/hc.rs`.\n- IMPORTANT: `gen_data(_, 0)` yields a `Vec` with a dangling pointer and some C paths\n  dereference `src` even for size 0. Define a local `gen_src()` helper that always makes a real\n  allocation with >= 64 readable zero bytes past `len`, and use it for every buffer handed to the\n  libraries (`tests/hc.rs` and `tests/block_decompress.rs` already do this — copy that helper).\n\n## The C API — read `c_src/include/lz4frame.h`, `lz4frame_static.h` and `c_src/src/lz4frame.c`\nYou MUST define the Rust `#[repr(C)]` mirrors of these structs EXACTLY (field order, types,\npadding) by reading the header:\n`LZ4F_frameInfo_t`, `LZ4F_preferences_t`, `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`,\n`LZ4F_CustomMem` (in lz4frame_static.h). All the enums are C `int`-sized. `LZ4F_errorCode_t` is\n`size_t`. Verify field-by-field; a wrong struct layout will produce fake \"divergences\".\n\nPublic entry points to cover (all are exported; confirm with `nm -D`):\n`LZ4F_isError LZ4F_getErrorName LZ4F_getErrorCode LZ4F_getVersion LZ4F_getBlockSize\nLZ4F_compressionLevel_max LZ4F_compressFrameBound LZ4F_compressFrame LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict\nLZ4F_createCDict LZ4F_createCDict_advanced LZ4F_freeCDict\nLZ4F_createCompressionContext LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced LZ4F_freeCompressionContext\nLZ4F_compressBegin LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce\nLZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict LZ4F_compressBegin_internal LZ4F_compressBound\nLZ4F_compressUpdate LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate LZ4F_flush LZ4F_compressEnd\nLZ4F_createDecompressionContext LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced\nLZ4F_freeDecompressionContext LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext\nLZ4F_headerSize LZ4F_getFrameInfo LZ4F_decompress LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`\n\n## tests/frame.rs — one `#[test]` per CONFIGS row group, named `rowNNN_...`\nConfiguration axes that MUST be crossed (the C branches on all of them):\n`blockSizeID` in {0,4,5,6,7}; `blockMode` in {0 blockLinked, 1 blockIndependent};\n`contentChecksumFlag` in {0,1}; `blockChecksumFlag` in {0,1}; `contentSize` in {0, exact};\n`dictID` in {0, 0xDEADBEEF}; `compressionLevel` in {-5,-1,0,1,2,3,6,9,10,11,12,13,100}\n(the C picks a fast `LZ4_stream_t` ctx below 2 and an HC ctx at >= 2);\n`autoFlush` in {0,1}; `favorDecSpeed` in {0,1}; `stableSrc` in {0,1}; `stableDst` in {0,1};\n`skipChecksums` in {0,1}.\n\n- row100: `LZ4F_compressFrame` with `prefsPtr == NULL` x src shapes/sizes.\n- row101: `LZ4F_compressFrame` blockSizeID x blockMode.\n- row102: full 2x2 of contentChecksumFlag x blockChecksumFlag.\n- row103: contentSize {0, exact} x dictID {0, 0xDEADBEEF}.\n- row104: the full compressionLevel list.\n- row105: favorDecSpeed x level {1,9,12}.\n- row106: autoFlush x blockSizeID {4,7}.\n- row107: src sizes {0,1,64,65535,65536,262144,1048577} vs blockSizeID (crossing block boundaries).\n- row108: the FULL cross-product sweep blockSizeID x blockMode x contentChecksum x blockChecksum\n  x level {1,9,12} (keep src modest so it finishes).\n- row109: `LZ4F_compressBegin` + ONE `LZ4F_compressUpdate` + `LZ4F_compressEnd`, all prefs axes as row108.\n- row110: begin + MANY `compressUpdate` calls with UNIFORM chunk sizes {1,2,3,7,64,1000,65536} + end.\n- row111: begin + MANY `compressUpdate` calls with RANDOM chunk sizes + end (tmpBuff accumulation).\n- row112: begin + updates with explicit `LZ4F_flush` interleaved at random points + end.\n- row113: `LZ4F_compressOptions_t.stableSrc` 0 vs 1.\n- row114: `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` (stored blocks) with blockIndependent, chunk-size sweep.\n- row115: `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` and `LZ4F_compressUpdate` MIXED within one frame (this forces\n  the internal `LZ4F_flush` at lz4frame.c:1013).\n- row116/117: `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` and `_usingDictOnce`, dictSize {1,64,1024,65535,65536,70000}.\n- row118: `LZ4F_createCDict` + `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict`, dict sweep x level {1,9,12} x blockMode.\n- row119: `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` (with an all-NULL `LZ4F_CustomMem`) + `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict`.\n- row120: `LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced` + ONE cctx REUSED across many frames.\n- row121: `LZ4F_compressBound` / `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` srcSize sweep x all valid blockSizeID\n  x autoFlush x blockChecksum (compare the returned sizes exactly).\n- row122: `LZ4F_getBlockSize` for {0,4,5,6,7}.\n- row123: `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`, `LZ4F_getVersion`.\n- row124: one-shot `LZ4F_decompress` of every frame produced above.\n- row125: `LZ4F_headerSize` + `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` on every row108 frame variant (7/11/15/19-byte headers).\n- row126: `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` called BEFORE any decompress, then decoding continues from there.\n- row127: `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` called mid-frame (after the header was consumed by `LZ4F_decompress`).\n- row128: `LZ4F_decompress` with src fed in FIXED chunks {1,2,3,4,5,7,11,15,19,20,33,64,1000}\n  (this splits the frame header, the 4-byte block headers and the checksums).\n- row129: src fed in RANDOM chunk sizes.\n- row130: dst offered in FIXED small chunks {1,2,3,7,64,1000} (exercises tmpOut buffering).\n- row131: dst offered in RANDOM chunk sizes.\n- row132: BOTH src and dst chunked randomly, honouring the returned `nextSrcSizeHint`.\n- row133: `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t.stableDst` 0 vs 1.\n- row134: `skipChecksums` 0 vs 1 on frames that DO carry content and/or block checksums.\n- row135: blockLinked frames chunked so matches reach back into the `tmpOutBuffer` history.\n- row136: frames containing STORED (uncompressed) blocks from row114.\n- row137: several frames concatenated and decoded on ONE dctx.\n- row138: a skippable frame (magic 0x184D2A50..0x184D2A5F + 4-byte LE size + payload) followed by a real frame.\n- row139: an empty frame (0 bytes of content) with every checksum combination.\n- row140: `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict` matching rows 116-119, with chunked src.\n- row141: `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` mid-frame, then decode a fresh frame.\n- row142: `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced` + ONE dctx REUSED across many frames.\n- row143: CROSS-DECODE — a frame produced by C decoded by Rust, and a frame produced by Rust\n  decoded by C; both must yield the original bytes.\n\nFor every call compare the C and Rust return value AND all produced bytes byte-for-byte, and also\nassert the decompressed result equals the original input.\n\n## tests/frame_errors.rs — one `#[test]` per ERRORS.md row, named `errNNN_...`\nRead `ERRORS.md` rows 125-203 in the crate root and implement EXACTLY those triggers.\n`LZ4F_errorCode_t` is `size_t` and error N is `(size_t)-N` = `lz4f_err(N)`. Assert the C and Rust\nreturn the SAME error code (not merely \"both failed\"). Highlights you must get right:\n- `LZ4F_getBlockSize` with blockSizeID in {1,2,3}, > 7, and NEGATIVE (out-of-range enum values\n  passed across FFI — C enums accept any int) => `lz4f_err(2)`; 0 => 65536; {4,5,6,7} => valid sizes.\n- `LZ4F_isError` for {0,1,23,24,25, (usize)-1, -23, -24, -25}; `LZ4F_getErrorName` for a non-error\n  code => \"Unspecified error code\", and for every ordinal 1..=23 => the matching string (compare\n  the C strings byte-for-byte via `CStr`); `LZ4F_getErrorCode`.\n- `LZ4F_createCompressionContext(NULL, ...)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; version != 100 => 0 (NOT validated).\n- `LZ4F_freeCompressionContext(NULL)` / `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext(NULL)` => 0.\n- `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext(NULL, ...)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; version != 100 => 0.\n- `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` on a MID-FRAME dctx returns the internal `dStage` number (a small\n  positive value, NOT an error) — assert C and Rust return the same number.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin` with dstCapacity 0..18 => `lz4f_err(11)`; exactly 19 => success.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin` with prefs.blockSizeID in {1,2,3,8} is NOT rejected — it SUCCEEDS and\n  `maxBlockSize` silently becomes `(size_t)-2`. Assert both return the same success value.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` with `dictSize > INT_MAX` => `lz4f_err(4)`. (Pass a huge size with\n  a real small buffer — the check happens before any read.)\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` / `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` on a cctx that was never `compressBegin`'d, and\n  again after a successful `compressEnd` => `lz4f_err(20)`.\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` with dstCapacity one below `LZ4F_compressBound(...)` => `lz4f_err(11)`;\n  exactly at the bound => success. `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` with dstCapacity < srcSize => `lz4f_err(11)`.\n- `LZ4F_flush` on an uninitialized cctx (tmpInSize == 0) => 0, NOT an error. With buffered data and\n  cStage != 1 => `lz4f_err(20)`. dstCapacity < tmpInSize+8 => `lz4f_err(11)`.\n- `LZ4F_compressEnd` dstCapacity too small for the endMark => `lz4f_err(11)`; with\n  contentChecksumEnabled needing 8 => `lz4f_err(11)`; declared `contentSize` != bytes actually fed\n  => `lz4f_err(14)`; on a fresh never-begun cctx => 4 (succeeds).\n- `LZ4F_compressBound`/`LZ4F_compressFrameBound` with an INVALID blockSizeID return a huge garbage\n  value (the C does not error-check `LZ4F_getBlockSize` there) — assert C and Rust produce the\n  IDENTICAL garbage.\n- `LZ4F_compressFrame` with dstCapacity < `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` => `lz4f_err(11)`; exactly at it => success.\n- `LZ4F_headerSize`: NULL src => `lz4f_err(15)`; srcSize 0..4 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic =>\n  `lz4f_err(13)`; skippable magic (all 16 values 0x184D2A50..5F) => 8; valid => 7/11/15/19.\n- `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`: srcSize < 5 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic => `lz4f_err(13)`; partial header\n  (>=5 but < hSize) => `lz4f_err(12)`; FLG bit1 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; FLG version field in {0,2,3}\n  => `lz4f_err(6)`; BD bit7 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; BD blockSizeID in {0,1,2,3} => `lz4f_err(2)`;\n  BD low nibble != 0 => `lz4f_err(8)`; wrong header-checksum byte => `lz4f_err(17)`;\n  called after feeding a PARTIAL header to `LZ4F_decompress` => `lz4f_err(19)`.\n  In each case also assert `*srcSizePtr` is set identically (the C zeroes it on these errors).\n  Build these headers BY HAND (magic + FLG + BD + optional 8-byte contentSize + optional 4-byte\n  dictID + header-checksum byte `(XXH32(hdr, n, 0) >> 8) & 0xFF`, using the library's own\n  `LZ4_XXH32` to compute it) so each field is corrupted in isolation.\n- `LZ4F_decompress`: srcSize 0 on a fresh dctx => 7 (a hint, not an error); every header error\n  above forwarded; block header size > maxBlockSize => `lz4f_err(2)`; corrupt compressed block\n  payload => `lz4f_err(16)`; wrong block checksum on a COMPRESSED block => `lz4f_err(7)`; wrong\n  block checksum on an UNCOMPRESSED/stored block => `lz4f_err(7)`; wrong content checksum =>\n  `lz4f_err(18)`; declared contentSize != regenerated bytes => `lz4f_err(14)`; truncated frame =>\n  a non-zero hint and no error; `*dstSizePtr` too small => partial output and no error.\n  Produce a VALID frame with the C library first, then corrupt exactly one field/byte for each row.\n- ALSO cover the generic boundaries: a large sweep of RANDOM/FUZZED byte strings fed to\n  `LZ4F_decompress` and `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` (a few thousand, fixed seed, various lengths) asserting\n  C and Rust always agree on the return code and on all output bytes; and out-of-range enum values\n  for `blockMode`, `contentChecksumFlag`, `blockChecksumFlag`, `frameType` (e.g. 2, 7, -1, 99999)\n  passed through `LZ4F_preferences_t` — the C silently MASKS these rather than rejecting them, so C\n  and Rust must agree on the resulting frame bytes (ERRORS.md row 203).\n- `LZ4F_createCDict(dict, 0)` and `LZ4F_freeCDict(NULL)`.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`. Do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`,\n   `tests/block_compress.rs`, `tests/block_decompress.rs`, `tests/hc.rs`,\n   `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n2. Beware DANGLING POINTERS in your own test code: cctx/dctx/CDict keep raw pointers into your\n   buffers; any `Vec` whose address the library retains MUST outlive every later call.\n   Never pass the pointer of a zero-capacity `Vec`.\n3. Keep total runtime under ~5 minutes per test binary (debug build). Prune the big cross-products\n   with modest source sizes rather than by dropping axes.\n4. Build/iterate with `timeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"` then\n   `timeout 600 cargo test --test frame 2>&1 | tail -40` and likewise for `--test frame_errors`.\n   Iterate until BOTH compile and RUN.\n5. If C and Rust genuinely DIVERGE: the C is ALWAYS correct. Fix the RUST implementation in\n   `src/lz4frame.rs` (or `src/lz4.rs` / `src/lz4hc.rs` / `src/xxhash.rs`) to match C exactly.\n   Never weaken, delete, `#[ignore]` or skip a test; never change an expected value to match Rust.\n   Real bug classes already found in this project: (i) Rust panicking \"attempt to subtract/add with\n   overflow\" where C does signed `ptrdiff_t` pointer arithmetic or relies on U32 wraparound — fix\n   with `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add` after confirming against the C source; (ii) a restore\n   statement executed twice on an error path.\n6. FINAL REPORT must state: (a) exact test names created in each file, (b) the pass/fail counts\n   from your last actual `cargo test` run of BOTH binaries, (c) EVERY divergence found with the\n   precise `src/*.rs` edit (file + line + before/after), (d) anything you could NOT get passing and why.\nDo not claim success without having actually run both test binaries."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BWPsptqTHXBbb5EJiTT6UL","session_id":"cf344e3a-451b-4037-95c8-f04f4dd0216c","uuid":"b38f3ee2-5863-4279-973b-7d6b9228b48f","timestamp":"2026-08-14T19:32:14.957Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lz4frame diff tests"}
