-a4a9-d825e0f51b4f","timestamp":"2026-08-14T20:22:31.798Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Mleh93/translated_rust\n\nWrite TWO new files:\n- `tests/lz4file.rs` — differential tests for lz4file.c (CONFIGS.md rows 144-150 AND ERRORS.md rows 204-230)\n- `tests/block_errors.rs` — ERROR-PATH differential tests for lz4.c / lz4hc.c / xxhash.c (ERRORS.md rows 1-124)\n\nBoth compare the C `.so` against the Rust `.so` through their exported symbols only.\n\n## Harness (already exists — read `tests/common/mod.rs` FIRST; do NOT modify it)\n- `mod common; use common::*;`\n- `sym!(name, \"C_SYMBOL\", FnType);` declares `name.0` = C fn, `name.1` = Rust fn; call as `name.0(args)` inside `unsafe`.\n- Helpers: `Rng::new(seed)`, `rng.range(lo,hi)`, `rng.below(n)`, `rng.next_u8/u32/u64`, `rng.fill`,\n  `gen_data(Shape, len, &mut rng)`, `ALL_SHAPES`, `KEY_LENS`, `SMALL_LENS`,\n  `assert_bytes_eq`, `assert_ret_eq`, `assert_out_eq`, `assert_sz_eq`,\n  `is_lz4f_error(code)`, `lz4f_err(n)` (= `(size_t)-n`), `Aligned::new(n)` + `.ptr()`,\n  `SIZEOF_LZ4_STREAM_T` (16416), `SIZEOF_LZ4_STREAMHC_T` (262200),\n  `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` (0x7E000000), `LZ4_ACCELERATION_MAX` (65537), `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX` (19).\n- Copy style/patterns from the existing `tests/block_compress.rs`, `tests/block_decompress.rs`, `tests/hc.rs`.\n- IMPORTANT: `gen_data(_, 0)` yields a `Vec` with a dangling pointer and several C paths dereference\n  `src` even at size 0. Copy the `gen_src()` helper from `tests/hc.rs` (always a real allocation with\n  >= 64 readable zero bytes past `len`) and use it for every buffer handed to the libraries.\n\n## FILE 1: tests/lz4file.rs\nRead `c_src/include/lz4file.h` and `c_src/src/lz4file.c`. Exported symbols:\n`LZ4F_readOpen LZ4F_read LZ4F_readClose LZ4F_writeOpen LZ4F_write LZ4F_writeClose`.\nSignatures:\n```\nLZ4F_errorCode_t LZ4F_readOpen(LZ4_readFile_t** lz4fRead, FILE* fp);\nsize_t           LZ4F_read(LZ4_readFile_t* lz4fRead, void* buf, size_t size);\nLZ4F_errorCode_t LZ4F_readClose(LZ4_readFile_t* lz4fRead);\nLZ4F_errorCode_t LZ4F_writeOpen(LZ4_writeFile_t** lz4fWrite, FILE* fp, const LZ4F_preferences_t* prefsPtr);\nsize_t           LZ4F_write(LZ4_writeFile_t* lz4fWrite, const void* buf, size_t size);\nLZ4F_errorCode_t LZ4F_writeClose(LZ4_writeFile_t* lz4fWrite);\n```\nYou need `FILE*` handles: declare `extern \"C\" { fn fopen(path: *const c_char, mode: *const c_char) -> *mut c_void; fn fclose(f: *mut c_void) -> c_int; fn fflush(f:*mut c_void)->c_int; }`\nand use real temp files under `std::env::temp_dir()` with unique names. Delete them at the end.\nCRITICAL: the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` are linked against the SAME libc, so a `FILE*` from\n`fopen` works with both — but use a SEPARATE `FILE*` (and a separate temp file) for the C run and\nthe Rust run, then compare the two files' BYTES.\nDefine the `#[repr(C)]` `LZ4F_preferences_t`/`LZ4F_frameInfo_t` mirrors by reading\n`c_src/include/lz4frame.h` field by field (a wrong layout produces fake divergences).\n\nTests (one `#[test]` per row group):\n- row144: `LZ4F_writeOpen`(prefs = NULL) + many `LZ4F_write` + `LZ4F_writeClose`, write chunk sizes\n  {1,2,7,64,1000,65536,1MB}; compare the two output files byte-for-byte AND both return values.\n- row145: same over blockSizeID {0,4,5,6,7} x blockMode {0,1} x contentChecksumFlag {0,1} x\n  blockChecksumFlag {0,1} x compressionLevel {1,9,12}.\n- row146: RANDOM write chunk sizes, total sizes that cross block boundaries.\n- row147: `LZ4F_readOpen` + many `LZ4F_read` + `LZ4F_readClose` over the row145 files, read chunk\n  sizes {1,2,7,64,1000,1MB}; compare all decoded bytes and every return value; assert the decoded\n  content equals the original.\n- row148: RANDOM read chunk sizes.\n- row149: CROSS round trip — the file written via the C `.so` read back via the Rust `.so`, and vice versa.\n- row150: a file containing MULTIPLE concatenated frames, and a file with trailing garbage after a\n  complete frame.\n- ERRORS.md rows 204-230 (put them in this same file as `errNNN_...` tests):\n  `LZ4F_readOpen` with fp NULL => `lz4f_err(21)`; with the out-pointer NULL => `lz4f_err(21)`;\n  a file SHORTER than 19 bytes (even a valid short frame!) => `lz4f_err(23)`; a file already at EOF\n  => `lz4f_err(23)`; >= 19 bytes with bad magic => `lz4f_err(13)`; with FLG reserved bit set =>\n  `lz4f_err(8)`; with a bad header checksum => `lz4f_err(17)`; with a bad FLG version => `lz4f_err(6)`.\n  `LZ4F_read` with a NULL handle => `lz4f_err(21)`; NULL buf => `lz4f_err(21)`; size 0 => 0;\n  reading past EOF of a complete frame => 0 (no error); corrupt payload mid-file => the forwarded\n  decompress error (same code from both).\n  `LZ4F_readClose(NULL)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; on a truncated frame => 0.\n  `LZ4F_writeOpen` fp NULL => `lz4f_err(21)`; out-pointer NULL => `lz4f_err(21)`;\n  `prefsPtr->frameInfo.blockSizeID` not in {0,4,5,6,7} (use 1,2,3,8,-1) => `lz4f_err(2)`;\n  prefsPtr NULL => 0; a READ-ONLY `FILE*` (opened \"rb\") so the header `fwrite` fails => `lz4f_err(22)`.\n  `LZ4F_write` NULL handle / NULL buf => `lz4f_err(21)`; size 0 => 0; success => returns `size`\n  (the UNCOMPRESSED count).\n  `LZ4F_writeClose(NULL)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; after a previous failed `LZ4F_write` => 0 (the C masks\n  the latched error); normal close => 0.\n\n## FILE 2: tests/block_errors.rs\nRead `ERRORS.md` rows 1-124 in the crate root and implement EXACTLY those triggers, one `#[test]`\nper row (or per tight group), named `errNN_...`. Assert C and Rust return the SAME sentinel, not\nmerely \"both failed\". Key points:\n- `LZ4_compressBound` / `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` over negatives, 0, 15, 16, LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE-1/\n  /+1, i32::MIN, i32::MAX and ~2000 random i32s.\n- `LZ4_compress_default`/`_fast` with `srcSize < 0` and `srcSize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` => 0. These\n  checks happen BEFORE `src` is read, so pass a small real buffer with a bogus huge/negative size.\n- `srcSize == 0` with `dstCapacity <= 0` => 0; with `dstCapacity >= 1` => 1 and `dst[0] == 0`.\n- acceleration clamping: `< 1` (0, -1, i32::MIN) must produce output byte-identical to\n  `acceleration == 1`; `> 65537` identical to `65537`.\n- `LZ4_compress_destSize` with `targetDstSize < 1` => 0; `*srcSizePtr < 0` => 0.\n- `LZ4_initStream` / `LZ4_initStreamHC`: NULL buffer => NULL; size one byte BELOW\n  `sizeof` (16415 / 262199) => NULL; MISALIGNED buffer (offset the pointer by 1..7) => NULL;\n  exactly `sizeof` and aligned => non-NULL.\n- `LZ4_freeStream(NULL)`, `LZ4_freeStreamDecode(NULL)`, `LZ4_freeStreamHC(NULL)`, `LZ4_freeHC(NULL)` => 0.\n- `LZ4_loadDict`/`LZ4_loadDictSlow`: dictSize 0..7 and negatives => 0; > 65536 => 65536; 8 and\n  65536 boundaries => those values.\n- `LZ4_saveDict`: > 65536 clamps; negative clamps; > the stream's dictSize clamps; 0 => 0.\n- `LZ4_decompress_safe`: `src == NULL` => -1; `dstCapacity < 0` => -1; `dstCapacity == 0` with a\n  non-canonical input => -1; `dstCapacity == 0, srcSize == 1, src[0] == 0` => 0; `srcSize == 0`\n  with `dstCapacity != 0` => -1.\n- MALFORMED-INPUT rows 34-42: build a VALID compressed block with the C compressor, then corrupt it\n  in each specific way — truncate the extended literal-length varint, truncate the extended\n  match-length varint, set an offset larger than the available history, set offset 0, make the\n  literal run overrun the input, make it overrun the output, put a match in the final 5 bytes\n  (LASTLITERALS), and give a dstCapacity one byte below the true decoded size. Assert the C and\n  Rust return the SAME negative value (the C returns `-(bytes consumed at error) - 1`, so the exact\n  magnitude matters). Also fuzz ~20000 random byte strings of assorted lengths through\n  `LZ4_decompress_safe`, `_safe_partial`, `_decompress_fast`, `LZ4_uncompress`,\n  `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize`, `_safe_usingDict` and `_safe_partial_usingDict` and assert\n  identical return values AND identical output bytes every time.\n- `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial` with `min(targetOutputSize, dstCapacity) == 0` => 0; negative\n  arguments => -1; `targetOutputSize > dstCapacity`; truncated input (silent partial success).\n- `LZ4_decompress_fast` rows 47-52: literal/match length overrunning the output, offset too large,\n  a match ending inside LASTLITERALS, and `originalSize` below the true size => -1.\n- `LZ4_setStreamDecode` with a negative dictSize => 1; with (NULL, 0) => 1.\n- `LZ4_attach_dictionary(working, NULL)` (detach) and with a dict stream whose dictSize is 0\n  (silently not attached) — assert the subsequent compression output matches the no-dict case\n  identically in both libraries.\n- HC rows 70-109: `LZ4_compress_HC` with `srcSize < 0`/`> MAX` => 0; dstCapacity too small => 0;\n  dstCapacity 0 => 0; `compressionLevel < 1` byte-identical to level 9; `> 12` identical to level 12;\n  level 1 ACCEPTED (valid `lz4mid` output, NOT clamped to 2); `srcSize == 0`.\n  `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC` with NULL/misaligned state => 0;\n  `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset` with a misaligned state => 0.\n  `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize` with `targetDstSize < 1` => 0. `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` with a too\n  small dstCapacity => 0. `LZ4_compress_HC_continue_destSize` with `targetDestSize < 1` => 0.\n  `LZ4_loadDictHC` dictSize {0,1,3,4,8,9,>64KB}. `LZ4_saveDictHC` maxDictSize {<4, >64KB, > prefixSize}.\n  `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` with a NULL/misaligned state => 1 (INVERTED convention: 1 = error), and\n  with a valid aligned state => 0.\n  `LZ4_setCompressionLevel` clamping (<1 => 9, >12 => 12) and `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed` with\n  nonzero values (1, -1, 12345 all behave as 1) — verify via the resulting compressed bytes.\n  `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` after a compression that returned <= 0 (the `dirty` flag) — output must\n  then equal a fresh stream's in both.\n  `LZ4_sizeofState`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamState`, `LZ4_sizeofStateHC`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC`,\n  `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max` (note: the symbol is `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`, there is no\n  `LZ4_compressionLevel_max`).\n- xxhash rows 110-124: `LZ4_XXH32_update(state, NULL, n)` and `LZ4_XXH64_update(state, NULL, n)` =>\n  `XXH_ERROR` == 1 (for several `n` incl. 0 and 100); `len == 0` with non-NULL input => 0 and the\n  digest unchanged; `LZ4_XXH32_freeState(NULL)` / `LZ4_XXH64_freeState(NULL)` => 0;\n  `LZ4_XXH32/64_reset` with extreme seeds => 0; `LZ4_XXH32/64(NULL, 0, seed)` => a valid hash equal\n  to the empty-input hash; `digest()` on a state fed nothing; canonical round trips; `LZ4_XXH_versionNumber` == 605.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`. Do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`,\n   `tests/block_compress.rs`, `tests/block_decompress.rs`, `tests/hc.rs`,\n   `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n   Another agent is concurrently creating `tests/frame.rs` and `tests/frame_errors.rs` — do NOT\n   touch those two files.\n2. Do NOT write tests for the cases listed in the \"Appendix — C paths that are undefined behaviour\"\n   section at the end of `ERRORS.md` (NULL derefs etc.): the C segfaults there, so they are not\n   differentially testable. Everything ABOVE the appendix must be covered.\n3. Beware DANGLING POINTERS in your own test code: LZ4 streams keep raw pointers into your buffers;\n   any `Vec` whose address a stream retains MUST outlive every later call on that stream.\n4. Keep each test binary's runtime under ~5 minutes in the debug build.\n5. Build/iterate with `timeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"` then\n   `timeout 600 cargo test --test lz4file 2>&1 | tail -40` and `--test block_errors`.\n   Iterate until BOTH compile and RUN.\n6. If C and Rust genuinely DIVERGE: the C is ALWAYS correct. Fix the RUST implementation in\n   `src/*.rs` to match C exactly. Never weaken, delete, `#[ignore]` or skip a test; never change an\n   expected value to match Rust. Real bug classes already found here: Rust panicking \"attempt to\n   subtract/add with overflow\" where C does signed `ptrdiff_t` pointer arithmetic or relies on U32\n   wraparound (fix with `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add` after confirming against the C source).\n7. FINAL REPORT must state: (a) exact test names created in each file, (b) the pass/fail counts from\n   your last actual `cargo test` run of BOTH binaries, (c) EVERY divergence found with the precise\n   `src/*.rs` edit (file + line + before/after), (d) anything you could NOT get passing and why.\nDo not claim success without having actually run both test binaries.","agentId":"a485730ccdddc1582","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files are written and passing, and no pre-existing suite regressed.\n\n## (a) Test names created\n\n**`tests/lz4file.rs`** (15 tests) — CONFIGS.md rows 144-150 + ERRORS.md rows 204-230\n`row144_write_prefs_null_chunk_sweep`, `row145_write_config_matrix`, `row146_write_random_chunks`, `row147_read_chunk_sweep`, `row148_read_random_chunks`, `row149_cross_round_trip`, `row150_multiframe_and_trailing_garbage`, `err204_205_read_open_null_params`, `err206_207_read_open_short_file_and_eof`, `err208_211_read_open_bad_header`, `err212_216_read_errors`, `err217_218_read_close`, `err219_223_write_open`, `err224_227_write`, `err228_230_write_close`\n\n**`tests/block_errors.rs`** (49 tests) — ERRORS.md rows 1-124, all covered\n`err01_03_compress_bound`, `err04_05_compress_bad_src_size`, `err06_07_compress_empty_src`, `err08_09_compress_dst_too_small`, `err10_11_acceleration_clamping`, `err12_14_compress_dest_size`, `err15_18_init_stream`, `err19_20_free_null`, `err21_24_load_dict`, `err25_28_save_dict`, `err29_33_decompress_safe_degenerate`, `err34_35_truncated_varints`, `err36_37_bad_offsets`, `err38_39_literal_overruns`, `err40_41_lastliterals_and_short_dst`, `err42_fuzz_all_decoders`, `err43_46_decompress_safe_partial`, `err47_52_decompress_fast`, `err53_54_deprecated_decoder_wrappers`, `err55_58_decoder_ring_buffer_size`, `err59_60_set_stream_decode`, `err61_decompress_safe_continue_corrupt`, `err62_63_decompress_safe_using_dict`, `err64_65_attach_dictionary`, `err66_67_compress_fast_continue`, `err68_compress_force_ext_dict`, `err69_sizeof_state`, `err70_73_init_stream_hc`, `err74_77_compress_hc_bad_args`, `err78_80_compress_hc_level_clamping`, `err81_compress_hc_empty_src`, `err82_84_ext_state_hc`, `err85_87_compress_hc_dest_size`, `err88_89_compress_hc_continue`, `err90_93_load_dict_hc`, `err94_96_save_dict_hc`, `err97_98_free_hc_null`, `err99_100_reset_stream_state_hc`, `err101_103_set_level_and_favor`, `err104_reset_stream_hc_fast_dirty`, `err105_106_attach_hc_dictionary`, `err107_deprecated_hc_oneshots`, `err108_109_sizeof_hc_and_level_max`, `err110_113_xxh_update_null_and_zero`, `err114_115_xxh_free_state_null`, `err116_117_xxh_reset_seeds`, `err118_121_xxh_empty_input`, `err122_123_xxh_canonical_round_trip`, `err124_xxh_version_number`\n\n## (b) Last actual `cargo test` results\n- `cargo test --test block_errors` → **49 passed; 0 failed** (2.88 s)\n- `cargo test --test lz4file` → **15 passed; 0 failed** (38.94 s)\n- Regression checks (unmodified suites, after my `src/` edit): `block_compress` 16/16, `block_decompress` 21/21, `xxhash` 8/8, `hc` 20/20 — all pass.\n\n## (c) Divergence found and fixed\nOne real Rust bug, in `src/lz4frame.rs`. The C computes `size_t copySize = 64 KB - dctx->tmpOutSize` and *relies on the `size_t` wraparound*, zeroing it immediately afterwards via `if (dctx->tmpOutSize > 64 KB) copySize = 0;` (c_src/src/lz4frame.c:1561 and :2091). Rust panicked `attempt to subtract with overflow` (an abort, since the cdylib can't unwind through `extern \"C\"`) whenever a block larger than 64 KB was buffered — reproduced by `row147`/`row148` with `blockSizeID` 5/6/7.\n\n- `src/lz4frame.rs:1380` (`LZ4F_updateDict`, `withinTmp` branch)\n  - before: `let mut copySize = 64 * 1024 - d.tmpOutSize;`\n  - after: `let mut copySize = (64 * 1024usize).wrapping_sub(d.tmpOutSize);`\n- `src/lz4frame.rs:1533` (`LZ4F_decompress`, `dstage_flushOut` dict-preservation tail)\n  - before: `let mut copySize = 64 * 1024 - d.tmpOutSize;`\n  - after: `let mut copySize = (64 * 1024usize).wrapping_sub(d.tmpOutSize);`\n\n(Each got a two-line comment citing the C.) No other divergence surfaced — including the 20 000-string × 7-entry-point decoder fuzz, which matched return values *and* full destination buffers every time.\n\n## (d) Things worth knowing (nothing left unpassing)\nThree ERRORS.md expectations are wrong about the C; I asserted what the C actually does (rule 6) and documented each in-place:\n- **row 230** — `LZ4F_writeClose` on success returns `LZ4F_compressEnd`'s byte count (4, or 8 with a content checksum, more with a buffered tail), **not** `0`; it never resets `ret`. `0` is only returned on the row-229 latched-error path.\n- **row 65** — attaching a `dictSize == 0` stream is *not* byte-identical to no-dict: the `currentOffset == 0` guard bumps `currentOffset` to 64 KB, flipping `noDictIssue`→`dictSmall`. I assert C==Rust and prove no dictionary was consulted (the block decodes with the plain decoder). `attach(NULL)` *is* byte-identical.\n- **row 37** — a bare `offset == 0` is **not** rejected by `LZ4_decompress_safe` (`match == op`, so `match + dictSize < lowPrefix` is false); it self-copies. Both the benign case and an offset-0 case that trips `LASTLITERALS` are tested.\n\nAlso worth noting: **row 80** — levels 1 and 2 share `lz4mid` in `k_clTable`, so level 1 == level 2 output; \"not clamped\" is proven against level 9 instead. **row 106** needs the *working* stream to hold ≥ 64 KB of *contiguous* history for the attached dict to be dropped (a non-contiguous block would clear `dictCtx` via `LZ4HC_setExternalDict` and prove nothing) — the test is built that way. **row 229** uses `/dev/full` (the buffered 7-byte header write succeeds, the ~64 KB flush inside `LZ4F_write` fails with ENOSPC), the only portable way to make `LZ4F_write`'s `fwrite` fail. `LZ4_decompress_fast` is fuzzed with `originalSize >= 0` only; a negative value writes arbitrarily far past `dst` in the C and is in the UB appendix."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":2954092,"totalTokens":344533,"totalToolUseCount":102,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":341156,"output_tokens":2563,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":812},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":6,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":84,"editFileCount":12,"linesAdded":2430,"linesRemoved":88,"otherToolCount":0}}}
