XED chunks {1,2,3,4,5,7,11,15,19,20,33,64,1000} (splits the\n  frame header, the 4-byte block headers and the checksums).\n- row129 src in RANDOM chunk sizes. row130 dst in FIXED small chunks {1,2,3,7,64,1000} (tmpOut\n  buffering). row131 dst in RANDOM chunk sizes. row132 BOTH src and dst chunked randomly, honouring\n  the returned `nextSrcSizeHint`.\n- row133 `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t.stableDst` 0 vs 1.\n- row134 `skipChecksums` 0 vs 1 on frames that DO carry content and/or block checksums.\n- row135 blockLinked frames chunked so matches reach back into the `tmpOutBuffer` history.\n- row136 frames containing STORED (uncompressed) blocks from row114.\n- row137 several frames concatenated, decoded on ONE dctx.\n- row138 a skippable frame (magic 0x184D2A50..0x184D2A5F + 4-byte LE size + payload) then a real frame.\n- row139 an empty frame (0 content bytes) with every checksum combination.\n- row140 `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict` matching rows 116-119, with chunked src.\n- row141 `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` mid-frame, then decode a fresh frame.\n- row142 `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced` + ONE dctx REUSED across many frames.\n- row143 CROSS-DECODE: a frame produced by C decoded by Rust, and one produced by Rust decoded by C;\n  both must yield the original bytes.\n\nCompare the C and Rust return value AND all produced bytes byte-for-byte on every call, and assert\nthe decompressed result equals the original input.\n\n## tests/frame_errors.rs — one `#[test]` per ERRORS.md row, named `errNNN_...`\nRead `ERRORS.md` rows 125-203 in the crate root and implement EXACTLY those triggers. Error N is\n`(size_t)-N` = `lz4f_err(N)`. Assert C and Rust return the SAME code (not merely \"both failed\").\nMust-get-right highlights:\n- `LZ4F_getBlockSize` with blockSizeID {1,2,3}, > 7, and NEGATIVE (out-of-range enum values across\n  FFI — C enums accept any int) => `lz4f_err(2)`; 0 => 65536; {4,5,6,7} => 65536/262144/1048576/4194304.\n- `LZ4F_isError` for {0,1,23,24,25,(usize)-1,-23,-24,-25}; `LZ4F_getErrorName` for a non-error code\n  => \"Unspecified error code\" and for every ordinal 1..=23 => the matching string (compare the C\n  strings byte-for-byte via `CStr`); `LZ4F_getErrorCode`.\n- `LZ4F_createCompressionContext(NULL,..)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; version != 100 => 0 (NOT validated).\n- `LZ4F_freeCompressionContext(NULL)` / `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext(NULL)` => 0.\n- `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext(NULL,..)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; version != 100 => 0.\n- `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` on a MID-FRAME dctx returns the internal `dStage` NUMBER (small\n  positive, not an error) — assert C and Rust return the same number.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin` dstCapacity 0..18 => `lz4f_err(11)`; exactly 19 => success.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin` with prefs.blockSizeID in {1,2,3,8}: NOT rejected — it SUCCEEDS and\n  `maxBlockSize` silently becomes `(size_t)-2`. Assert both return the same success value.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` with `dictSize > INT_MAX` => `lz4f_err(4)` (the check precedes any\n  read, so pass a huge size with a real small buffer).\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` / `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` on a cctx never `compressBegin`'d, and again\n  after a successful `compressEnd` => `lz4f_err(20)`.\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` with dstCapacity one below `LZ4F_compressBound(..)` => `lz4f_err(11)`;\n  exactly at the bound => success. `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` with dstCapacity < srcSize => `lz4f_err(11)`.\n- `LZ4F_flush` on an uninitialized cctx (tmpInSize == 0) => 0, NOT an error; with buffered data and\n  cStage != 1 => `lz4f_err(20)`; dstCapacity < tmpInSize+8 => `lz4f_err(11)`.\n- `LZ4F_compressEnd`: dstCapacity too small for the endMark => `lz4f_err(11)`; with\n  contentChecksumEnabled needing 8 => `lz4f_err(11)`; declared `contentSize` != bytes actually fed\n  => `lz4f_err(14)`; on a fresh never-begun cctx => 4 (succeeds).\n- `LZ4F_compressBound`/`LZ4F_compressFrameBound` with an INVALID blockSizeID return a huge garbage\n  value (the C does not error-check `LZ4F_getBlockSize` there) — assert C and Rust produce the\n  IDENTICAL garbage.\n- `LZ4F_compressFrame` dstCapacity < `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` => `lz4f_err(11)`; exactly at it => success.\n- `LZ4F_headerSize`: NULL src => `lz4f_err(15)`; srcSize 0..4 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic =>\n  `lz4f_err(13)`; skippable magic (ALL 16 values 0x184D2A50..5F) => 8; valid => 7/11/15/19.\n- `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`: srcSize < 5 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic => `lz4f_err(13)`; partial header\n  (>=5 but < hSize) => `lz4f_err(12)`; FLG bit1 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; FLG version field in {0,2,3} =>\n  `lz4f_err(6)`; BD bit7 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; BD blockSizeID in {0,1,2,3} => `lz4f_err(2)`; BD low\n  nibble != 0 => `lz4f_err(8)`; wrong header-checksum byte => `lz4f_err(17)`; called after feeding a\n  PARTIAL header to `LZ4F_decompress` => `lz4f_err(19)`. In each case ALSO assert `*srcSizePtr` is\n  set identically (the C zeroes it on these errors).\n  Build these headers BY HAND (magic + FLG + BD + optional 8-byte LE contentSize + optional 4-byte LE\n  dictID + header-checksum byte `(XXH32(hdr, n, 0) >> 8) & 0xFF`, computed with the library's own\n  `LZ4_XXH32`) so each field is corrupted in isolation.\n- `LZ4F_decompress`: srcSize 0 on a fresh dctx => 7 (a hint, not an error); every header error above\n  forwarded; block header size > maxBlockSize => `lz4f_err(2)`; corrupt compressed block payload =>\n  `lz4f_err(16)`; wrong block checksum on a COMPRESSED block => `lz4f_err(7)`; wrong block checksum\n  on an UNCOMPRESSED/stored block => `lz4f_err(7)`; wrong content checksum => `lz4f_err(18)`;\n  declared contentSize != regenerated bytes => `lz4f_err(14)`; truncated frame => a non-zero hint and\n  no error; `*dstSizePtr` too small => partial output and no error.\n  Produce a VALID frame with the C library first, then corrupt exactly one field/byte per row.\n- ALSO cover generic boundaries: a large sweep of RANDOM/FUZZED byte strings (a few thousand, fixed\n  seed, assorted lengths) fed to `LZ4F_decompress` and `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`, asserting C and Rust\n  always agree on the return code and on all output bytes; and OUT-OF-RANGE ENUM values for\n  `blockMode`, `contentChecksumFlag`, `blockChecksumFlag`, `frameType` (e.g. 2, 7, -1, 99999) passed\n  via `LZ4F_preferences_t` — the C silently MASKS these rather than rejecting, so C and Rust must\n  agree on the resulting frame bytes (ERRORS.md row 203).\n- `LZ4F_createCDict(dict, 0)` and `LZ4F_freeCDict(NULL)`.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`. Do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`,\n   `tests/block_compress.rs`, `tests/block_decompress.rs`, `tests/hc.rs`, `tests/lz4file.rs`,\n   `tests/block_errors.rs`, `tests/xxhash.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n2. Beware DANGLING POINTERS in your own test code: cctx/dctx/CDict keep raw pointers into your\n   buffers; any `Vec` whose address the library retains MUST outlive every later call. Never pass the\n   pointer of a zero-capacity `Vec`.\n3. Keep each test binary under ~5 minutes in the debug build. Prune big cross-products with modest\n   source sizes rather than by dropping axes.\n4. Build/iterate with `timeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"`, then\n   `timeout 600 cargo test --test frame 2>&1 | tail -40` and `timeout 600 cargo test --test frame_errors 2>&1 | tail -40`.\n   Iterate until BOTH compile and RUN.\n5. If C and Rust genuinely DIVERGE: the C is ALWAYS correct. Fix the RUST implementation in\n   `src/lz4frame.rs` (or `src/lz4.rs` / `src/lz4hc.rs` / `src/xxhash.rs`) to match C exactly. Never\n   weaken, delete, `#[ignore]` or skip a test; never change an expected value to match Rust.\n   If you find that an ERRORS.md row misstates what the C does, follow the C, assert the C's ACTUAL\n   behaviour, and REPORT the discrepancy in your final report (do not edit ERRORS.md).\n   Real bug classes already found in this project: (i) Rust panicking \"attempt to subtract/add with\n   overflow\" where C does signed `ptrdiff_t` pointer arithmetic or relies on `size_t`/`U32`\n   wraparound — fix with `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add` after confirming against the C source\n   (already fixed at `src/lz4frame.rs:1382` and `:1535`, `src/lz4.rs` dictEnd-match,\n   `src/lz4hc.rs:588` and `:1117`); (ii) a restore statement executed twice on an error path.\n6. FINAL REPORT must state: (a) exact test names created in each file, (b) the pass/fail counts from\n   your last actual `cargo test` run of BOTH binaries, (c) EVERY divergence found with the precise\n   `src/*.rs` edit (file + line + before/after), (d) every ERRORS.md row whose stated expectation\n   did not match the C, (e) anything you could NOT get passing and why.\nDo not claim success without having actually run both test binaries.","uuid":"a8ed0eec-bf97-4194-8f28-ba86ad2fe851","session_id":"cf344e3a-451b-4037-95c8-f04f4dd0216c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Mleh93/translated_rust\n\nWrite TWO new files:\n- `tests/frame.rs` — VALID-PATH differential tests for lz4frame.c (CONFIGS.md rows 100-143)\n- `tests/frame_errors.rs` — ERROR-PATH differential tests for lz4frame.c (ERRORS.md rows 125-203)\n\nBoth compare the C `.so` against the Rust `.so` through their exported symbols only.\n\n## Harness (already exists — read `tests/common/mod.rs` FIRST; do NOT modify it)\n- `mod common; use common::*;`\n- `sym!(name, \"C_SYMBOL\", FnType);` declares `name.0` = C fn, `name.1` = Rust fn; call as `name.0(args)` inside `unsafe`.\n- Helpers: `Rng::new(seed)`, `rng.range(lo,hi)`, `rng.below(n)`, `rng.next_u8/u32/u64`, `rng.fill`,\n  `gen_data(Shape, len, &mut rng)`, `ALL_SHAPES`, `KEY_LENS`, `SMALL_LENS`,\n  `assert_bytes_eq`, `assert_ret_eq`, `assert_out_eq`, `assert_sz_eq(cn,cbuf,rn,rbuf,ctx)`,\n  `is_lz4f_error(code) -> bool` (mirrors `LZ4F_isError`), `lz4f_err(n) -> usize` (= `(size_t)-n`),\n  `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX` (19), `LZ4F_VERSION` (100), `LZ4F_MAGICNUMBER` (0x184D2204).\n- STUDY the existing `tests/block_compress.rs`, `tests/hc.rs`, `tests/lz4file.rs` and\n  `tests/block_errors.rs` for the exact established style. `tests/lz4file.rs` ALREADY defines\n  `#[repr(C)]` mirrors of `LZ4F_preferences_t` / `LZ4F_frameInfo_t` — reuse that exact layout\n  (re-derive it from `c_src/include/lz4frame.h` to be sure).\n- IMPORTANT: `gen_data(_, 0)` yields a `Vec` with a dangling pointer and several C paths dereference\n  `src` even at size 0. Copy the `gen_src()` helper from `tests/hc.rs` (always a real allocation with\n  >= 64 readable zero bytes past `len`) and use it for every buffer handed to the libraries.\n\n## The C API — read `c_src/include/lz4frame.h`, `lz4frame_static.h`, `c_src/src/lz4frame.c`\nDefine `#[repr(C)]` mirrors EXACTLY (field order, types, padding) for:\n`LZ4F_frameInfo_t`, `LZ4F_preferences_t`, `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`,\n`LZ4F_CustomMem` (lz4frame_static.h). All enums are C `int`-sized; `LZ4F_errorCode_t` is `size_t`.\nVerify field-by-field — a wrong layout produces fake \"divergences\".\n\nEntry points to cover (all exported; confirm with `nm -D c_src/build/liblz4.so`):\n`LZ4F_isError LZ4F_getErrorName LZ4F_getErrorCode LZ4F_getVersion LZ4F_getBlockSize\nLZ4F_compressionLevel_max LZ4F_compressFrameBound LZ4F_compressFrame LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict\nLZ4F_createCDict LZ4F_createCDict_advanced LZ4F_freeCDict\nLZ4F_createCompressionContext LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced LZ4F_freeCompressionContext\nLZ4F_compressBegin LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce\nLZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict LZ4F_compressBound\nLZ4F_compressUpdate LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate LZ4F_flush LZ4F_compressEnd\nLZ4F_createDecompressionContext LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced\nLZ4F_freeDecompressionContext LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext\nLZ4F_headerSize LZ4F_getFrameInfo LZ4F_decompress LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`\n\n## tests/frame.rs — one `#[test]` per row group, named `rowNNN_...`\nAxes the C branches on, all of which MUST be crossed:\n`blockSizeID` {0,4,5,6,7}; `blockMode` {0 linked, 1 independent}; `contentChecksumFlag` {0,1};\n`blockChecksumFlag` {0,1}; `contentSize` {0, exact}; `dictID` {0, 0xDEADBEEF};\n`compressionLevel` {-5,-1,0,1,2,3,6,9,10,11,12,13,100} (the C picks a fast `LZ4_stream_t` ctx below 2\nand an HC ctx at >= 2); `autoFlush` {0,1}; `favorDecSpeed` {0,1}; `stableSrc` {0,1};\n`stableDst` {0,1}; `skipChecksums` {0,1}.\n\n- row100 `LZ4F_compressFrame` with `prefsPtr == NULL` x src shapes/sizes.\n- row101 blockSizeID x blockMode. row102 contentChecksum x blockChecksum (full 2x2).\n- row103 contentSize {0,exact} x dictID {0,0xDEADBEEF}. row104 the full compressionLevel list.\n- row105 favorDecSpeed x level {1,9,12}. row106 autoFlush x blockSizeID {4,7}.\n- row107 src sizes {0,1,64,65535,65536,262144,1048577} vs blockSizeID (crossing block boundaries).\n- row108 FULL cross-product blockSizeID x blockMode x contentChecksum x blockChecksum x level {1,9,12}.\n- row109 `compressBegin` + ONE `compressUpdate` + `compressEnd`, prefs axes as row108.\n- row110 begin + MANY `compressUpdate` with UNIFORM chunk sizes {1,2,3,7,64,1000,65536} + end.\n- row111 begin + MANY `compressUpdate` with RANDOM chunk sizes + end (tmpBuff accumulation).\n- row112 begin + updates with explicit `LZ4F_flush` interleaved at random points + end.\n- row113 `LZ4F_compressOptions_t.stableSrc` 0 vs 1.\n- row114 `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` (stored blocks), blockIndependent, chunk-size sweep.\n- row115 `uncompressedUpdate` and `compressUpdate` MIXED in ONE frame (forces the internal\n  `LZ4F_flush` at lz4frame.c:1013).\n- row116/117 `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` and `_usingDictOnce`, dictSize {1,64,1024,65535,65536,70000}.\n- row118 `LZ4F_createCDict` + `compressBegin_usingCDict`, dict sweep x level {1,9,12} x blockMode.\n- row119 `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` (all-NULL `LZ4F_CustomMem`) + `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict`.\n- row120 `LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced` + ONE cctx REUSED across many frames.\n- row121 `LZ4F_compressBound` / `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` srcSize sweep x every valid blockSizeID\n  x autoFlush x blockChecksum (compare returned sizes exactly).\n- row122 `LZ4F_getBlockSize` {0,4,5,6,7}. row123 `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`, `LZ4F_getVersion`.\n- row124 one-shot `LZ4F_decompress` of every frame produced above.\n- row125 `LZ4F_headerSize` + `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` on every row108 variant (7/11/15/19-byte headers).\n- row126 `getFrameInfo` BEFORE any decompress, then decoding continues from there.\n- row127 `getFrameInfo` mid-frame (after the header was consumed by `LZ4F_decompress`).\n- row128 `LZ4F_decompress` src fed in FIXED chunks {1,2,3,4,5,7,11,15,19,20,33,64,1000} (splits the\n  frame header, the 4-byte block headers and the checksums).\n- row129 src in RANDOM chunk sizes. row130 dst in FIXED small chunks {1,2,3,7,64,1000} (tmpOut\n  buffering). row131 dst in RANDOM chunk sizes. row132 BOTH src and dst chunked randomly, honouring\n  the returned `nextSrcSizeHint`.\n- row133 `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t.stableDst` 0 vs 1.\n- row134 `skipChecksums` 0 vs 1 on frames that DO carry content and/or block checksums.\n- row135 blockLinked frames chunked so matches reach back into the `tmpOutBuffer` history.\n- row136 frames containing STORED (uncompressed) blocks from row114.\n- row137 several frames concatenated, decoded on ONE dctx.\n- row138 a skippable frame (magic 0x184D2A50..0x184D2A5F + 4-byte LE size + payload) then a real frame.\n- row139 an empty frame (0 content bytes) with every checksum combination.\n- row140 `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict` matching rows 116-119, with chunked src.\n- row141 `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` mid-frame, then decode a fresh frame.\n- row142 `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced` + ONE dctx REUSED across many frames.\n- row143 CROSS-DECODE: a frame produced by C decoded by Rust, and one produced by Rust decoded by C;\n  both must yield the original bytes.\n\nCompare the C and Rust return value AND all produced bytes byte-for-byte on every call, and assert\nthe decompressed result equals the original input.\n\n## tests/frame_errors.rs — one `#[test]` per ERRORS.md row, named `errNNN_...`\nRead `ERRORS.md` rows 125-203 in the crate root and implement EXACTLY those triggers. Error N is\n`(size_t)-N` = `lz4f_err(N)`. Assert C and Rust return the SAME code (not merely \"both failed\").\nMust-get-right highlights:\n- `LZ4F_getBlockSize` with blockSizeID {1,2,3}, > 7, and NEGATIVE (out-of-range enum values across\n  FFI — C enums accept any int) => `lz4f_err(2)`; 0 => 65536; {4,5,6,7} => 65536/262144/1048576/4194304.\n- `LZ4F_isError` for {0,1,23,24,25,(usize)-1,-23,-24,-25}; `LZ4F_getErrorName` for a non-error code\n  => \"Unspecified error code\" and for every ordinal 1..=23 => the matching string (compare the C\n  strings byte-for-byte via `CStr`); `LZ4F_getErrorCode`.\n- `LZ4F_createCompressionContext(NULL,..)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; version != 100 => 0 (NOT validated).\n- `LZ4F_freeCompressionContext(NULL)` / `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext(NULL)` => 0.\n- `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext(NULL,..)` => `lz4f_err(21)`; version != 100 => 0.\n- `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` on a MID-FRAME dctx returns the internal `dStage` NUMBER (small\n  positive, not an error) — assert C and Rust return the same number.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin` dstCapacity 0..18 => `lz4f_err(11)`; exactly 19 => success.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin` with prefs.blockSizeID in {1,2,3,8}: NOT rejected — it SUCCEEDS and\n  `maxBlockSize` silently becomes `(size_t)-2`. Assert both return the same success value.\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` with `dictSize > INT_MAX` => `lz4f_err(4)` (the check precedes any\n  read, so pass a huge size with a real small buffer).\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` / `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` on a cctx never `compressBegin`'d, and again\n  after a successful `compressEnd` => `lz4f_err(20)`.\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` with dstCapacity one below `LZ4F_compressBound(..)` => `lz4f_err(11)`;\n  exactly at the bound => success. `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` with dstCapacity < srcSize => `lz4f_err(11)`.\n- `LZ4F_flush` on an uninitialized cctx (tmpInSize == 0) => 0, NOT an error; with buffered data and\n  cStage != 1 => `lz4f_err(20)`; dstCapacity < tmpInSize+8 => `lz4f_err(11)`.\n- `LZ4F_compressEnd`: dstCapacity too small for the endMark => `lz4f_err(11)`; with\n  contentChecksumEnabled needing 8 => `lz4f_err(11)`; declared `contentSize` != bytes actually fed\n  => `lz4f_err(14)`; on a fresh never-begun cctx => 4 (succeeds).\n- `LZ4F_compressBound`/`LZ4F_compressFrameBound` with an INVALID blockSizeID return a huge garbage\n  value (the C does not error-check `LZ4F_getBlockSize` there) — assert C and Rust produce the\n  IDENTICAL garbage.\n- `LZ4F_compressFrame` dstCapacity < `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` => `lz4f_err(11)`; exactly at it => success.\n- `LZ4F_headerSize`: NULL src => `lz4f_err(15)`; srcSize 0..4 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic =>\n  `lz4f_err(13)`; skippable magic (ALL 16 values 0x184D2A50..5F) => 8; valid => 7/11/15/19.\n- `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`: srcSize < 5 => `lz4f_err(12)`; bad magic => `lz4f_err(13)`; partial header\n  (>=5 but < hSize) => `lz4f_err(12)`; FLG bit1 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; FLG version field in {0,2,3} =>\n  `lz4f_err(6)`; BD bit7 set => `lz4f_err(8)`; BD blockSizeID in {0,1,2,3} => `lz4f_err(2)`; BD low\n  nibble != 0 => `lz4f_err(8)`; wrong header-checksum byte => `lz4f_err(17)`; called after feeding a\n  PARTIAL header to `LZ4F_decompress` => `lz4f_err(19)`. In each case ALSO assert `*srcSizePtr` is\n  set identically (the C zeroes it on these errors).\n  Build these headers BY HAND (magic + FLG + BD + optional 8-byte LE contentSize + optional 4-byte LE\n  dictID + header-checksum byte `(XXH32(hdr, n, 0) >> 8) & 0xFF`, computed with the library's own\n  `LZ4_XXH32`) so each field is corrupted in isolation.\n- `LZ4F_decompress`: srcSize 0 on a fresh dctx => 7 (a hint, not an error); every header error above\n  forwarded; block header size > maxBlockSize => `lz4f_err(2)`; corrupt compressed block payload =>\n  `lz4f_err(16)`; wrong block checksum on a COMPRESSED block => `lz4f_err(7)`; wrong block checksum\n  on an UNCOMPRESSED/stored block => `lz4f_err(7)`; wrong content checksum => `lz4f_err(18)`;\n  declared contentSize != regenerated bytes => `lz4f_err(14)`; truncated frame => a non-zero hint and\n  no error; `*dstSizePtr` too small => partial output and no error.\n  Produce a VALID frame with the C library first, then corrupt exactly one field/byte per row.\n- ALSO cover generic boundaries: a large sweep of RANDOM/FUZZED byte strings (a few thousand, fixed\n  seed, assorted lengths) fed to `LZ4F_decompress` and `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`, asserting C and Rust\n  always agree on the return code and on all output bytes; and OUT-OF-RANGE ENUM values for\n  `blockMode`, `contentChecksumFlag`, `blockChecksumFlag`, `frameType` (e.g. 2, 7, -1, 99999) passed\n  via `LZ4F_preferences_t` — the C silently MASKS these rather than rejecting, so C and Rust must\n  agree on the resulting frame bytes (ERRORS.md row 203).\n- `LZ4F_createCDict(dict, 0)` and `LZ4F_freeCDict(NULL)`.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n1. Do NOT modify anything under `c_src/`. Do NOT modify `tests/common/mod.rs`,\n   `tests/block_compress.rs`, `tests/block_decompress.rs`, `tests/hc.rs`, `tests/lz4file.rs`,\n   `tests/block_errors.rs`, `tests/xxhash.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n2. Beware DANGLING POINTERS in your own test code: cctx/dctx/CDict keep raw pointers into your\n   buffers; any `Vec` whose address the library retains MUST outlive every later call. Never pass the\n   pointer of a zero-capacity `Vec`.\n3. Keep each test binary under ~5 minutes in the debug build. Prune big cross-products with modest\n   source sizes rather than by dropping axes.\n4. Build/iterate with `timeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"`, then\n   `timeout 600 cargo test --test frame 2>&1 | tail -40` and `timeout 600 cargo test --test frame_errors 2>&1 | tail -40`.\n   Iterate until BOTH compile and RUN.\n5. If C and Rust genuinely DIVERGE: the C is ALWAYS correct. Fix the RUST implementation in\n   `src/lz4frame.rs` (or `src/lz4.rs` / `src/lz4hc.rs` / `src/xxhash.rs`) to match C exactly. Never\n   weaken, delete, `#[ignore]` or skip a test; never change an expected value to match Rust.\n   If you find that an ERRORS.md row misstates what the C does, follow the C, assert the C's ACTUAL\n   behaviour, and REPORT the discrepancy in your final report (do not edit ERRORS.md).\n   Real bug classes already found in this project: (i) Rust panicking \"attempt to subtract/add with\n   overflow\" where C does signed `ptrdiff_t` pointer arithmetic or relies on `size_t`/`U32`\n   wraparound — fix with `wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_add` after confirming against the C source\n   (already fixed at `src/lz4frame.rs:1382` and `:1535`, `src/lz4.rs` dictEnd-match,\n   `src/lz4hc.rs:588` and `:1117`); (ii) a restore statement executed twice on an error path.\n6. FINAL REPORT must state: (a) exact test names created in each file, (b) the pass/fail counts from\n   your last actual `cargo test` run of BOTH binaries, (c) EVERY divergence found with the precise\n   `src/*.rs` edit (file + line + before/after), (d) every ERRORS.md row whose stated expectation\n   did not match the C, (e) anything you could NOT get passing and why.\nDo not claim success without having actually run both test binaries."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018sW7qJeRE7yaPd45kLYPUS","session_id":"cf344e3a-451b-4037-95c8-f04f4dd0216c","uuid":"fbd236f0-06e9-41e2-ac6e-1c709c56939b","timestamp":"2026-08-14T20:24:26.453Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lz4frame diff tests"}
