{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01RtrT8LzSpAnECREBgVYiYQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — Configuration-surface table (valid inputs)\n2\t\n3\tDerived mechanically from the branches the C actually takes. Axes were found by\n4\tgrepping the public headers for every runtime option/flag, and the `.c` files for\n5\tevery `if`/`switch` on those flags plus every input-shape special case.\n6\t\n7\t## Axes the C branches on\n8\t\n9\t**lz4.c block API**\n10\t- `tableType`: `byU16` iff `inputSize < LZ4_64Klimit` (65547), else `byU32`\n11\t  (`byPtr` is 32-bit-only, unreachable here) — lz4.c:1389/1396\n12\t- `dict` directive: `noDict` | `withPrefix64k` | `usingExtDict` | `usingDictCtx`\n13\t- `dictIssue`: `noDictIssue` | `dictSmall` (`dictSize < 64KB && dictSize < currentOffset`, lz4.c:1747)\n14\t- `limitedOutput`: `notLimited` (`dstCapacity >= LZ4_compressBound`) | `limitedOutput` | `fillOutput` (destSize)\n15\t- `acceleration`: 1 (default) | 2..65536 | 65537 (`LZ4_ACCELERATION_MAX`)\n16\t- input SHAPE: 0 | 1 | 12 (`< LZ4_minLength` 13) | 13 | 64 | 1024 | 65535\n17\t  (`LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX`) | 65536 | 65546/65547 (`LZ4_64Klimit` boundary) | 200000;\n18\t  incompressible (random) | highly compressible (runs) | mixed | long-match\n19\t- dictCtx bulk-copy threshold: `inputSize > 4096` (lz4.c:1762)\n20\t\n21\t**lz4hc.c**\n22\t- `cLevel` classes: 1-2 → `lz4mid` | 3-9 → HC chain | 10-12 → optimal parser\n23\t  (`LZ4HC_CLEVEL_OPT_MIN`); `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT` 9, `MAX` 12\n24\t- `favorDecSpeed`: 0 | 1 (only consulted at levels >= 10)\n25\t- `limit`: `notLimited` | `limitedOutput` | `fillOutput` (destSize entry points)\n26\t- dict source: none | `LZ4_loadDictHC` | `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary` | non-contiguous\n27\t  `continue` (`LZ4HC_setExternalDict`)\n28\t- state-compatibility straddle across the `lz4mid` boundary (lz4hc.c:1434)\n29\t\n30\t**lz4frame.c** (`LZ4F_preferences_t` / `LZ4F_frameInfo_t` / `LZ4F_compressOptions_t` /\n31\t`LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`)\n32\t- `blockSizeID`: 0 (`default`→64KB) | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7\n33\t- `blockMode`: `blockLinked` (0) | `blockIndependent` (1)\n34\t- `contentChecksumFlag`: 0 | 1 ; `blockChecksumFlag`: 0 | 1\n35\t- `contentSize`: 0 (absent) | exact | (mismatch → error, see ERRORS.md)\n36\t- `dictID`: 0 | non-zero ; `frameType`: `LZ4F_frame` | `LZ4F_skippableFrame`\n37\t- `compressionLevel`: <2 → fast `LZ4_stream_t` ctx | >=2 → HC ctx (lz4frame.c:705)\n38\t- `autoFlush`: 0 | 1 ; `favorDecSpeed`: 0 | 1 ; `stableSrc`: 0 | 1 ; `stableDst`: 0 | 1\n39\t- `skipChecksums`: 0 | 1\n40\t- API shape: one-shot `LZ4F_compressFrame` | `compressBegin`/`compressUpdate`*/\n41\t  `flush`/`compressEnd` | `uncompressedUpdate` (stored blocks) | mixed\n42\t  `compressUpdate`+`uncompressedUpdate`\n43\t- dict shape: none | `compressBegin_usingDict` | `_usingDictOnce` | `_usingCDict` |\n44\t  `compressFrame_usingCDict`\n45\t- decode shape: one-shot | chunked src (chunk sizes crossing the 4/7/11/15/19-byte\n46\t  header, the 4-byte block header, the 4-byte checksums) | chunked dst | both\n47\t\n48\t**lz4file.c**: `writeOpen` prefs (all frame axes) × write chunk size;\n49\t`readOpen` × read chunk size.\n50\t\n51\t**xxhash.c**: `XXH32` (16-byte buffer) / `XXH64` (32-byte buffer); one-shot vs\n52\tstreaming; chunk sizes crossing the internal buffer boundary; seed; length shape.\n53\t\n54\t## Rows\n55\t\n56\tEach row is exercised with MANY randomized inputs (fixed seed, `tests/common/mod.rs`\n57\t`Rng`), comparing the C `.so` and Rust `.so` byte-for-byte.\n58\t\n59\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n60\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n61\t| **xxhash** | | | |\n62\t| 1 | `LZ4_XXH32` | one-shot, len 0..300 sweep × seeds {0,1,0x9E3779B1,UINT32_MAX} | [x] |\n63\t| 2 | `LZ4_XXH64` | one-shot, len 0..300 sweep × seeds {0,1,0x9E3779B185EBCA87,UINT64_MAX} | [x] |\n64\t| 3 | `LZ4_XXH32` | one-shot, large len {1KB,