{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KYGXMbLfbocTQ8wHJwxcBg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ERRORS.md — Error-surface table (LZ4 v1.10.0 + xxHash 0.6.5)\n2\t\n3\tDerived mechanically from `c_src/src/*.c` by grepping every `RETURN_ERROR*`,\n4\t`FORWARD_IF_ERROR`, `return 0/-1/NULL` failure return, `assert`, explicit range\n5\tcheck, null check, and min/max constant.\n6\t\n7\tBuild context that scopes this table (from `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`):\n8\t`-DXXH_NAMESPACE=LZ4_ -DLZ4_HEAPMODE=0 -DLZ4F_HEAPMODE=0`, no `-DNDEBUG`,\n9\tno `-DLZ4_DEBUG`. Therefore `assert()` in `lz4.c`/`lz4hc.c`/`lz4frame.c` expands\n10\tto `((void)0)` (LZ4's own `assert` shim) and is NOT a runtime rejection, while\n11\t`LZ4HC_HEAPMODE` defaults to 1 so `lz4hc.c` heap-allocation failures ARE compiled.\n12\t\n13\t`LZ4F_errorCode_t` is `size_t`; error N is returned as `(size_t)-N`.\n14\tOrdinals: `maxBlockSize_invalid 2, blockMode_invalid 3, parameter_invalid 4,\n15\tcompressionLevel_invalid 5, headerVersion_wrong 6, blockChecksum_invalid 7,\n16\treservedFlag_set 8, allocation_failed 9, srcSize_tooLarge 10,\n17\tdstMaxSize_tooSmall 11, frameHeader_incomplete 12, frameType_unknown 13,\n18\tframeSize_wrong 14, srcPtr_wrong 15, decompressionFailed 16,\n19\theaderChecksum_invalid 17, contentChecksum_invalid 18,\n20\tframeDecoding_alreadyStarted 19, compressionState_uninitialized 20,\n21\tparameter_null 21, io_write 22, io_read 23, maxCode 24`.\n22\t\n23\tTest file: `tests/errors.rs`. Every row below has a differential test that calls\n24\tBOTH the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` and asserts identical error/sentinel values.\n25\t\n26\t## lz4.c — block API\n27\t\n28\t| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n29\t|---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n30\t| 1 | `LZ4_compressBound` | `isize < 0` | `0` |\n31\t| 2 | `LZ4_compressBound` | `isize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` (2113929216) | `0` |\n